      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkshire%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Browns Settlement, the town was founded in 1808 from Union in Broome County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkshire%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Royce House and Farm Complex in Berkshire earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkshire%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "East Berkshire United Methodist Church, built in the 19th century, was added to the National Register in 1984.",
